# Minimal documented model-listener deployment of the pinned 0.4.39 image.

version boot
  The image accepts the v0.3.0 configuration schema used by the accepted August deployment.
listeners/type boot
  type:model exposes the LLM gateway rather than adding an agent-orchestration hop.
listeners/port bind
  12000 is the model listener port; 10000 is occupied by the separately generated prompt listener.
mount /app/plano_config.yaml boot
  The image reads this path without entrypoint arguments or PLANO_CONFIG_FILE. The file is read-only.
model_providers/model upstream
  Normal provider/model prefixes select the released adapter. The August OpenAI, Anthropic and
  Gemini entries are retained. The documented amazon_bedrock provider adds its omitted Converse
  upstream; it is not a replacement for another provider or a performance override.
model_providers/base_url upstream
  Redirect every configured backend to the mock.
model_providers/access_key boot
  Dummy upstream key required by the deployment; the mock accepts it.
model_providers/default upstream
  The existing OpenAI default model is retained. Each measured cell selects its explicit model.

No provider_interface override is needed for these recognized prefixes. No tracing override is
needed: config/envoy.template.yaml activates tracing only for an explicitly positive random_sampling.
The redundant random_sampling:0 was removed, leaving the shipped default behavior.

The source's hermesllm/src/clients/endpoints.rs accepts Chat, Responses and Messages ingress.
providers/id.rs::compatible_api_for_client selects native Responses for Responses-to-OpenAI,
Chat for Messages-to-OpenAI, native Messages for Messages-to-Anthropic and Converse for all three
client APIs to amazon_bedrock. Gemini uses Google's OpenAI-compatible endpoint, which is not the
native Gemini wire tested by this matrix. No native Gemini, Cohere or Bedrock ingress is registered.
Source: https://github.com/katanemo/plano/blob/b13ddd632bde1fea7678386c345665ea5fa671af/crates/hermesllm/src/providers/id.rs

Fresh single-request checks on the pinned image retain all three accepted August pairs, verify
Messages-to-Chat, and verify the three newly configured Converse pairs. Historical July process
exit observations do not establish a current failure; genuine failures in the field remain results.
